.TH SCOPELINK-CLI 1 "2026-08-12" "indi-scopelink 1.0" "INDI Drivers"
.SH NAME
scopelink-cli \- read and configure an Astrolabs ScopeLink controller from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scopelink-cli
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR device ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scopelink-cli
talks to a ScopeLink controller directly, without libindi, a client or a running INDI server in the way.
It exists mostly for support: "run this and send me what it prints" is a far shorter conversation than
talking somebody through a graphical client over email.
.PP
The driver must not be connected to the same port at the same time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " device"
Port to open. Defaults to
.IR /dev/ttyACM0 .
Prefer the per-unit name under
.IR /dev/serial/by-id/ ,
which does not renumber.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log every request and every response as hex, on standard error, along with the protocol layer's own
messages. This is what a capture for the driver's conformance vectors is taken from.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Identification, capabilities and one status sample.
.TP
.B status
One status sample.
.TP
.B parameters
Every configuration identifier this controller holds, with its value.
.TP
.BI export " file"
Write the whole configuration to
.IR file ,
in the format the vendor's Windows parameter editor reads and writes. Take one of these before changing
anything: it is the only backup of a unit's calibration.
.TP
.BI import " file"
Read
.I file
and write to the controller any value that differs. Values the connected generation does not hold are
skipped. Configuration lives in EEPROM, which has a finite number of write cycles, so only differences
are written.
.TP
.B faults
The fault store, with the freeze frame captured when each code was raised.
.TP
.B clear-faults
Clear every stored code, then read the store back. A code whose cause is still present reappears
immediately, which is the point of reading it back.
.TP
.B eeprom
The EEPROM wear counters.
.SH EXAMPLES
Identify whatever is on a port:
.PP
.RS
.B scopelink-cli --port /dev/ttyACM0 info
.RE
.PP
Back a unit's configuration up before changing it:
.PP
.RS
.B scopelink-cli --port /dev/serial/by-id/usb-STMicroelectronics_STM32_Virtual_ComPort_in_FS_Mode_205E35793630-if00 export before.did
.RE
.PP
Capture the wire traffic for a bug report:
.PP
.RS
.B scopelink-cli --port /dev/ttyACM0 --verbose info 2>capture.log
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when the command completed, non-zero when the controller could not be reached or did not answer
usefully.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR indi_scopelink (1),
.BR scopelink-simulator (1)
